course: dictionary
lesson: 15239
title: Sheared: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sheared is the past form of the verb shear. It can mean three different things, so context is the key. «The farmer sheared all the sheep before summer.» Here the clue is sheep: sheared means the wool was cut off.
explain: «Mum sheared the long grass with the garden shears.» The word shears is the clue. Sheared means cut with shears, or with another sharp tool.
explain: «The bolt sheared off when the crane pulled too hard.» Here there is no cutting at all. Sheared off means it broke off because a strong force pushed it sideways.
fact: Shear is a verb. Sheared is its past form, and shorn is another past form.
fact: «Sheared» can mean had the wool cut off, as with sheep.
fact: «Sheared» can also mean cut with shears or another sharp tool.
fact: «Sheared off» means broke off because of a strong force pushed sideways.
fact: In Australia, New Zealand and the UK, farmers shear their sheep about once a year.
exercise: «The farmers sheared the sheep in spring, so the wool could be sold.» What does sheared mean here? | *Had the wool cut off | Counted in a pen | Washed in a river | Fed with hay
exercise: «The metal pin sheared off when the wind pushed the gate hard.» What does sheared off mean? | Pulled out gently | *Broke off because of a strong sideways force | Painted bright red | Turned slowly in a circle
exercise: «Mum sheared the long grass with the garden shears.» Find and copy the word that names the tool. | long | grass | Mum | *shears
test: «After the bolt sheared off, the wheel fell.» Why did the bolt break? | *A strong sideways force | It was made of wool | It was painted too much | Someone sang to it
test: «The sheep were sheared in May, and their wool was packed into big sacks.» Which words tell you the wool was removed? | packed into big sacks | in May | big sacks | *The sheep were sheared
exam: «The sheep looked much smaller once they were sheared.» What has happened to the sheep? | They had a bath | They grew a longer coat | They were painted | *Their wool was cut off
